# ---------- Commerce (Production Launch Session 02) ----------
# ALL SERVER-ONLY. There is deliberately NO NEXT_PUBLIC Shopify variable any
# more: the browser never talks to Shopify, and the Admin token must never
# reach a client bundle.
#
# PRODUCTION FAILS CLOSED. With NODE_ENV=production and these unset, the app
# REFUSES to fall back to the mock commerce provider — mock checkout charges
# nobody but would write MOCK-* orders, purchase_completed events and
# conversion marks that every downstream system reports as real revenue.
# /api/checkout answers 503 and the server log names what is missing.
# PARTIAL configuration (one of the two) fails in EVERY environment.
# Leave BOTH unset for development/test mock commerce.
#
#   SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN     "your-store.myshopify.com" — no https://, no path
#   SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN  Admin API access token (shpat_…), scopes
#                            write_draft_orders AND read_orders (the latter is
#                            required by the Session 03 reconciliation sweep,
#                            which recovers payments whose webhook never
#                            arrived — nothing broader). Checkout creates a DRAFT ORDER
#                            priced by the BagDirect engine, because Shopify's
#                            Storefront cart cannot express a custom line price
#                            (docs/SHOPIFY_PRODUCTION.md §5).
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=
SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN=

# Webhook signing secret (Settings → Notifications → Webhooks, shown once).
# Required for PAID ORDER RECONCILIATION: every webhook is HMAC-verified
# before any parsing or database write, and an unset secret makes the endpoint
# fail closed (503) — paid orders are then NOT reconciled. Subscribe:
# orders/create, orders/paid, orders/cancelled, refunds/create → POST
# https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/shopify
SHOPIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional API-version pin. MUST be in SUPPORTED_SHOPIFY_API_VERSIONS
# (config/shopify.ts — currently 2026-07). An unsupported value fails LOUDLY;
# it never silently falls back. Upgrade: docs/SHOPIFY_PRODUCTION.md §12.
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=

# NOTE: Shopify variant ids are NOT env vars. They live in
# config/shopify.ts → SHOPIFY_MERCHANDISE_MAP, one per purchasable
# product·size·material·color. It ships EMPTY; an unmapped configuration
# fails checkout visibly and never falls back to another variant.

# ---------- Artwork object storage (Production Launch Session 02) ----------
# S3-compatible: AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, DO Spaces, MinIO.
# Server-only — the browser receives one short-lived signed URL for one
# server-chosen object key, and never learns the bucket or a credential.
#
# UNSET = artwork upload is unavailable and SAYS SO (503, "choose No logo").
# It never pretends an upload succeeded. PARTIAL configuration throws.
# Without it, printed products cannot be ordered — which is correct: a paid
# order whose logo went nowhere is worse than a refused one.
# Bucket must be PRIVATE (no public read). docs/ARTWORK_STORAGE.md.
ARTWORK_S3_ENDPOINT=
ARTWORK_S3_REGION=
ARTWORK_S3_BUCKET=
ARTWORK_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
ARTWORK_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Path-style addressing (MinIO and some R2 setups). Default: virtual-host style.
ARTWORK_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=

# ---------- Site domain (Production Launch Session 03) ----------
# THE canonical production domain. Drives canonical metadata, the sitemap,
# robots.txt, structured data and admin deep links.
#
# BUILD-TIME INLINED — changing it requires a REDEPLOY, not a restart.
#
# UNSET (or left as "example.com") = launch readiness reports BLOCKED, and
# robots.txt refuses crawling entirely rather than advertising a sitemap at a
# domain you do not own. `next build` still works, deliberately: missing owner
# input must never make the build impossible.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_DOMAIN=

# ---------- Pricing safety ----------
# Seed pricing renders with a visible "demo pricing" notice until this is
# explicitly set to false AND real prices are loaded.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_PRICING=true

# ---------- Analytics & ad conversions (Session 03) ----------
# ALL BUILD-TIME INLINED — a change requires a REDEPLOY.
#
# The purchase these deliver comes ONLY from an authoritative PAID order
# (Shopify webhook -> markOrderPaid -> the confirmation endpoint). It never
# fires from a created checkout, a redirect, a query parameter or the AI.
# Every one of them can fail without affecting the customer's order.
# docs/ANALYTICS_PRODUCTION.md.
#
# GTM set  -> GTM manages the tags; configure GA4/Ads inside GTM to trigger
#             on the `purchase` dataLayer event.
# GTM unset -> gtag.js is loaded directly for whichever ids are set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
# BOTH are required for a Google Ads conversion: the label is what addresses
# the conversion action (send_to = AW-XXXXXXXXX/label). An id without a label
# is reported as NOT configured.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_PURCHASE_LABEL=

# ---------- Meta ----------
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
# Server-only — Conversions API. DEFERRED this session and read by NO code
# today (docs/ANALYTICS_PRODUCTION.md §8). The browser Pixel already emits an
# eventID equal to the transaction id, so adding CAPI later is server-side only.
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
META_DATASET_ID=

# ---------- Database ----------
# Production/staging: a standard Postgres connection string. Migrations are
# applied explicitly there: `npm run db:migrate`.
# Unset (development/tests): an embedded PGlite Postgres self-migrates at
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR (default .data/pglite; tests use memory://). No setup needed.
DATABASE_URL=
PGLITE_DATA_DIR=

# ---------- First-party events ----------
# The storefront dual-writes selected analytics events to /api/events (our own
# database) in addition to the consent-gated GA4/Meta dataLayer. Set to false
# to disable first-party event persistence entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIRST_PARTY_EVENTS=true

# ---------- Quote intake ----------
# JSON POST target for custom-quote requests (helpdesk / Zapier / email service).
# Unset = requests log to the server console (development).
QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------- Human escalation delivery (Session 03) ----------
# Where an AI escalation goes. A generic JSON POST reaches a Slack workflow,
# Zapier/Make, email automation or a helpdesk intake URL without embedding any
# of them in the architecture. Falls back to QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL when unset.
#
# PERSISTENCE IS PRIMARY: every escalation is stored and visible at
# /admin/handoffs whether or not delivery succeeds. Unset means escalations are
# recorded but nobody is notified — reported as a warning on
# /admin/launch-readiness.
HUMAN_HANDOFF_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------- Monitoring & error tracking (Session 03) ----------
# Both optional; the app works fully with neither. Unexpected SERVER exceptions
# are always written to the structured log first, then delivered to whichever
# of these is configured. Expected business outcomes (below MOQ, 409 REPRICED,
# unmapped configuration, invalid input) are NEVER reported as errors.
#
# SENTRY_DSN uses Sentry's documented envelope ingest directly — no SDK, so no
# browser capture, no source maps, no tracing (docs/OBSERVABILITY.md §3).
SENTRY_DSN=
ERROR_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------- Rate limiting (Session 03) ----------
# Layer 1 (per-instance token bucket) is always on. Layer 2 is a durable shared
# counter in Postgres, so limits mean the same thing across instances.
# Defaults: ON in production, OFF in development/tests. Setting it false in
# production is a deliberate, documented downgrade.
#
# A store outage NEVER opens the gate: the per-instance limit still applies and
# the degradation is logged. LAYER 0 — platform/WAF rate limiting — is OWNER
# CONFIGURATION and is a launch requirement (docs/OBSERVABILITY.md §6).
RATE_LIMIT_DURABLE=
# Keyed hash for the network identity. A raw IP is NEVER persisted anywhere;
# only an HMAC digest reaches a counter key or a log line. Unset = an ephemeral
# per-process key, so network-scoped durable limits degrade to per-instance and
# nothing persisted can be correlated to a person even in principle.
# Production: set a long random string and rotate it like any secret.
RATE_LIMIT_IP_SALT=

# ---------- Artwork allowances (Session 03) ----------
# Bounds how many objects ONE anonymous session can create in your bucket.
# Rate limiting bounds the RATE; this bounds the TOTAL. Deliberately generous —
# a blocked customer is a lost order. Defaults: 25 files per 24 hours.
ARTWORK_MAX_UPLOADS_PER_SESSION=
ARTWORK_UPLOAD_WINDOW_HOURS=

# ---------- AI runtime (Session 04 — all OFF by default) ----------
# Master switch for lib/ai. Everything below is inert until this is "true".
# Commerce works fully with every AI flag off.
AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED=false
# Customer-facing "AI Packaging Expert" chat (Session 05): requires
# AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED=true + a provider key. Off = no chat UI, /api/ai/chat
# answers 503, storefront unaffected. Before enabling for customers, verify
# the configured model ids with `npm run ai:smoke` (credential-gated,
# never part of tests/build).
AI_SALES_ENABLED=false
# Customer Intelligence (Session 08): gates /admin/customer-intelligence and
# its processing endpoint. Deterministic metrics render with just this flag;
# AI classification of conversations additionally needs AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED
# + a provider key. Off = the admin surface 404s, commerce unaffected.
AI_CUSTOMER_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false
# Business Intelligence (Session 09): gates /admin/business-intelligence and
# the CEO-review endpoint. Deterministic business metrics render with just
# this flag + admin auth; the CEO review generation additionally needs
# AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED + a provider key and only ever runs from the explicit
# admin button. Off = the admin surface 404s, commerce unaffected.
AI_BUSINESS_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false
# AI Action Center (Session 10): gates /admin/ai-actions and its
# approve/reject/modify endpoints. The Guardrail Engine itself is ALWAYS
# active (every proposed action is evaluated regardless of this flag) — this
# only controls the admin surface. No AI call is made by this surface: it
# reads persisted CEO decisions and runs deterministic policy. Off = the
# admin surface 404s, commerce unaffected.
AI_ACTION_CENTER_ENABLED=false
# Experiment engine (Session 11): gates /admin/experiments, every experiment
# API route, and ALL traffic assignment + exposure recording. Off = no
# assignment, no exposure, control experience everywhere, and the storefront
# renders exactly as it did before Session 11 (statically where it was
# static). ON makes / and /products/[slug] render dynamically, so TOGGLING
# THIS FLAG REQUIRES A REBUILD/REDEPLOY — a build made with it off will never
# enrol anyone. Before running experiments in PRODUCTION you must also set
# GUARDRAIL_LIMITS.maximumExperimentTrafficPct in config/guardrails.ts: while
# it is null the launch route refuses in production (never assumes 100%).
EXPERIMENT_ENGINE_ENABLED=false
# CRO agent (Session 11): gates CRO proposal generation only. Needs
# AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED + a provider key, and only ever runs from the explicit
# admin button. Experiments run, measure and report normally with this off or
# with the provider down — active experiments never depend on the LLM.
AI_CRO_AGENT_ENABLED=false

# Pricing Intelligence dashboard (Session 12): gates
# /admin/pricing-intelligence and its API route (both 404 while off). Needs
# ADMIN_USER/ADMIN_PASSWORD. Every number on the page is deterministic — the
# dashboard needs NO AI configuration whatsoever.
PRICING_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false
# Pricing agent (Session 12): gates the pricing REVIEW generation only, and
# only ever runs from the explicit admin button. Needs AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED + a
# provider key. It cannot set a price — its output schema has no price field
# — and it cannot execute anything. With this off (or the provider down) the
# pricing dashboard is completely unaffected.
AI_PRICING_AGENT_ENABLED=false

# Google Ads Intelligence dashboard (Session 13): gates
# /admin/google-ads-intelligence, the connection test and the sync route (all
# 404 while off). Needs ADMIN_USER/ADMIN_PASSWORD. Every number on the page is
# deterministic and read from PERSISTED synced data — rendering it makes NO
# Google Ads API call. With this flag OFF, no Google Ads call is ever made.
GOOGLE_ADS_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false
# Google Ads agent (Session 13): gates the Google Ads REVIEW generation only,
# and only ever runs from the explicit admin button. Needs AI_RUNTIME_ENABLED
# + a provider key. The agent has NO tools and NO Google Ads access at all —
# its output schema has no budget, campaign-status, bid, keyword or ad field,
# so a campaign change is unrepresentable. With this off (or the provider
# down) the Google Ads dashboard is completely unaffected.
AI_GOOGLE_ADS_AGENT_ENABLED=false

# ---------- Google Ads API (Session 13 — READ-ONLY) ----------
# Server-only. NEVER NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never committed, never logged, never sent
# to a model, never stored in the database.
#
# This integration can ONLY read: it issues GAQL SELECT queries against
# GoogleAdsService:search and contains no code path that can construct a
# mutating endpoint. A read-only Google account is therefore sufficient — and
# is what you should use.
#
# Where each value comes from:
#   DEVELOPER_TOKEN  Google Ads API Center (must be approved for production;
#                    a test-mode token cannot read a production account)
#   CLIENT_ID/SECRET Google Cloud Console → OAuth 2.0 client (Desktop/Web)
#   REFRESH_TOKEN    OAuth consent for a user with READ access to the account,
#                    scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords
#   CUSTOMER_ID      The Google Ads account being reported on (dashes ok)
#   LOGIN_CUSTOMER_ID  ONLY if that account sits under a manager (MCC): the
#                    MANAGER's id, sent as the login-customer-id header
#
# Missing values are NOT an error: the dashboard shows NOT_CONNECTED, and the
# rest of the platform (storefront, AI Sales, checkout, every other
# intelligence layer) is entirely unaffected. NOT CONNECTED IS NEVER READ AS
# ZERO SPEND anywhere in the system.
GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=
GOOGLE_ADS_LOGIN_CUSTOMER_ID=
# Optional pin. MUST be a version in SUPPORTED_API_VERSIONS
# (config/google-ads.ts — currently v25). An unsupported value fails LOUDLY;
# it never silently falls back to an older version. Upgrade procedure:
# docs/GOOGLE_ADS_INTELLIGENCE.md §4.
GOOGLE_ADS_API_VERSION=

# Provider selection (configuration, not code). Implemented: anthropic.
# Interface-ready, not yet implemented: openai, gemini.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Server-only keys — NEVER NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never committed.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Model routing by workload class (LOW_COST: classification/extraction,
# STANDARD: customer-facing conversation, REASONING: business analysis).
# Defaults (in lib/ai/config.ts): haiku-4-5 / sonnet-5 / opus-5.
AI_MODEL_LOW_COST=
AI_MODEL_STANDARD=
AI_MODEL_REASONING=

# AI spend caps (USD, UTC windows). Unset = no cap (documented default).
# NOTE: budgets require pricing for the active models in config/ai-pricing.ts
# — budgets over unmeasurable spend fail closed.
AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=
AI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=

# Tuning (defaults in lib/ai/config.ts; normally leave unset):
# AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000       provider call timeout
# AI_PROVIDER_MAX_RETRIES=1         transport retries on 429/5xx
# AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=16000        per-call output cap (incl. thinking)
# AI_MAX_TOOL_CALLS_PER_TURN=8      tool-loop safety limits
# AI_MAX_MODEL_CALLS_PER_TURN=5
# AI_MAX_TURN_DURATION_MS=120000
# AI_STRUCTURED_RETRY_LIMIT=1

# ---------- Admin (Session 08 — first admin surface) ----------
# HTTP Basic credentials for /admin and /api/admin (proxy.ts + per-route
# checks). FAIL CLOSED: while unset, every admin path answers 404 — the
# surface does not exist. Set BOTH to enable. Use a long random password;
# rotate by changing the values (no session state to invalidate).
ADMIN_USER=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
